WEBVTT

01:04.147 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:08.943 --> 01:09.861
Well,

01:10.904 --> 01:12.238
we have a house

01:13.448 --> 01:14.908
and even a boat.

01:16.659 --> 01:18.161
This is insane.

01:20.330 --> 01:21.164
You happy?

01:21.247 --> 01:22.290
Yeah.

01:24.626 --> 01:25.877
I am, Gwan-sik.

01:36.429 --> 01:38.223
Uh, stop!

01:48.983 --> 01:52.695
It was our brightest season,
and it would never return.

01:55.198 --> 01:59.369
LIFE GOES ON AND ON

02:23.560 --> 02:25.979
HALLIM DISASTER RELIEF
DEPUTY CHIEF OH AE-SUN

02:33.611 --> 02:35.321
BABY FORMULA

02:47.375 --> 02:49.210
You've got to live up to your title.

02:49.836 --> 02:50.670
Okay?

02:56.759 --> 02:58.928
I'm the deputy chief, after all.

02:59.429 --> 03:02.015
Let's just add two more.

03:19.490 --> 03:21.242
Oh, for goodness' sake.

03:22.410 --> 03:26.873
I told you I'd give you candy
after your food was done, didn't I?

03:26.956 --> 03:29.167
Why don't you ever listen to Mommy?

03:29.751 --> 03:32.128
-Goodness gracious.
-Mommy, give me a hug.

03:32.212 --> 03:34.172
Give me a hug.

03:34.255 --> 03:38.676
Mommy, I want a hug.
Mommy, Mommy, give me a hug.

03:38.760 --> 03:40.470
Mommy! Mommy!

03:40.553 --> 03:43.556
Ms. Oh! Ms. Oh!
Geum-myeong is in trouble! She's hurt!

03:43.640 --> 03:45.141
-Mommy!
-What?

03:45.225 --> 03:46.476
Mommy!

03:49.145 --> 03:51.314
Is she bleeding? Tell me! Tell me!

03:52.065 --> 03:53.441
I don't know. It's this way.

03:55.193 --> 03:58.738
Auntie! Auntie!
Can you watch my kids for me?

03:58.821 --> 04:00.323
Huh?

04:33.523 --> 04:35.984
Are you the sea god's daughter? Are you?

04:36.067 --> 04:38.194
Look, even the dolphins are running away.

04:38.278 --> 04:40.154
How can you ride in a typhoon?

04:40.780 --> 04:43.366
It's the motorbike that hit me,
not the other way around.

04:44.784 --> 04:47.078
Jeju winds can flip over cars.

04:47.161 --> 04:49.872
Your little bike here
would flip over again and again.

04:50.373 --> 04:51.207
Gosh.

04:59.340 --> 05:00.216
Auntie!

05:02.593 --> 05:03.761
Auntie!

05:09.058 --> 05:10.226
Auntie!

05:11.394 --> 05:12.603
Where are the boys?

05:14.772 --> 05:16.607
Are they sleeping in our house?

05:16.691 --> 05:18.526
Huh? The boys?

05:28.411 --> 05:29.704
Eun-myeong!

05:31.414 --> 05:34.876
So why did you leave the boys behind?
It wasn't even a major accident.

05:35.460 --> 05:37.962
-Eun-myeong. Honey! Oh no.
-Eun-myeong!

05:38.046 --> 05:39.380
-Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

05:39.464 --> 05:41.299
-Dong-myeong!
-Honey!

05:42.508 --> 05:44.010
Dong-myeong!

05:44.093 --> 05:46.095
Eun-myeong! Eun-myeong!

05:47.180 --> 05:49.015
Eun-myeong! Eun-myeong!

05:56.356 --> 05:58.149
How many times did Grandma warn you

05:58.232 --> 06:01.194
that once the boys start running,
they'll go anywhere, huh?

06:01.277 --> 06:02.653
Hey, their shoes.

06:03.654 --> 06:05.281
Their shoes are not here.

06:06.240 --> 06:07.075
What?

06:07.909 --> 06:09.702
I'll go look in the cabbage field and…

06:09.786 --> 06:12.580
-Ae-sun, pay me for seaweed.
-…and, Mom, look around…

06:13.164 --> 06:15.917
I didn't harvest all the seaweed
I was going to

06:16.834 --> 06:18.920
because I found your biggest boy here.

06:19.003 --> 06:20.421
Goodness gracious.

06:20.922 --> 06:21.881
Oh!

06:22.382 --> 06:25.009
I told you not to move and stay here,
didn't I?

06:25.718 --> 06:29.889
He was standing alone on the seawall,
afraid and desperately looking for you.

06:29.972 --> 06:31.057
Why did you leave?

06:31.140 --> 06:33.643
Why did you go to
such a dangerous area alone?

06:34.143 --> 06:36.270
The truck auntie would've come for you.

06:36.354 --> 06:38.064
Why couldn't you just wait?

06:38.147 --> 06:39.232
Why?

06:39.315 --> 06:42.735
If you stand there,
the waves will swallow you up.

06:42.819 --> 06:45.363
Cows get swept up by Jeju typhoons.

06:45.446 --> 06:47.073
You have to be careful.

06:48.157 --> 06:49.367
Where's Dong-myeong?

06:52.662 --> 06:54.288
Where's Dong-myeong?

06:54.372 --> 06:55.206
At home.

06:55.957 --> 06:58.167
Wasn't Dong-myeong with you
this whole time?

07:00.378 --> 07:01.879
He's home!

07:04.882 --> 07:07.635
What are you telling me? Stop scaring me.

07:08.136 --> 07:10.304
Mommy, give me a hug.

07:10.388 --> 07:14.058
-Give me a hug. Mommy, I want a hug.
-Is she bleeding? Tell me. Tell me!

07:14.142 --> 07:16.769
Mommy. Mommy.

07:49.302 --> 07:50.428
Geum-myeong,

07:51.888 --> 07:53.347
go call the chief's office.

08:05.026 --> 08:07.069
Who can stop
the whims of summer?

08:07.570 --> 08:11.032
Yesterday, it was bright and sunny,
like a bride on her wedding day.

08:11.699 --> 08:14.744
And today, it gets aggressive
like when your wife loses her temper.

08:15.244 --> 08:17.455
At least you can always get
a new wife…

08:17.538 --> 08:19.499
…but when summer screws you over…

08:21.250 --> 08:22.168
Goddamn it.

08:22.251 --> 08:23.586
-Okay.
-Ow!

08:24.212 --> 08:26.214
Oh man.

08:26.714 --> 08:29.425
You can't build a barrier
by running your mouth, right?

08:30.051 --> 08:30.927
Gwan-sik!

08:31.010 --> 08:32.929
Gwan-sik!

08:39.602 --> 08:42.230
-Honey! Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

08:42.313 --> 08:43.606
Dong-myeong!

08:45.691 --> 08:47.235
Dong-myeong!

08:47.318 --> 08:48.736
Dong-myeong!

08:50.154 --> 08:51.489
-Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

08:51.572 --> 08:53.199
Yang Dong-myeong!

08:53.282 --> 08:54.659
Dong-myeong!

08:56.410 --> 08:58.246
Dong-myeong!

08:58.329 --> 08:59.539
Dong-myeong!

09:00.289 --> 09:01.832
Dong-myeong!

09:03.292 --> 09:04.168
Dong-myeong!

09:04.252 --> 09:05.920
Dong-myeong!

09:06.003 --> 09:08.381
-Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

09:08.464 --> 09:10.925
Dong-myeong!

09:12.718 --> 09:14.762
-Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

09:15.346 --> 09:19.100
Where did he go? Dong-myeong!

09:20.142 --> 09:21.686
Dong-myeong!

09:23.062 --> 09:25.231
Dong-myeong! Honey!

09:27.358 --> 09:29.819
Yang Dong-myeong! Honey!

09:29.902 --> 09:31.112
Where are you?

09:31.195 --> 09:32.196
Dong-myeong!

09:34.490 --> 09:35.866
Dong-myeong! Yang Dong-myeong!

09:35.950 --> 09:38.160
Please have mercy on us.
Please, dear Lord.

09:38.244 --> 09:40.997
Whatever it takes,
save the child for us, dear Lord.

09:41.080 --> 09:42.999
Just save my grandchild.

09:44.041 --> 09:45.668
Send our baby back to us.

09:47.211 --> 09:49.213
Please save the child. Please.

09:50.256 --> 09:52.550
It only takes a second to lose a child.

09:52.633 --> 09:54.135
Please save him. Save my grandbaby.

09:54.218 --> 09:56.804
Do you know what people
all over the world say

09:57.305 --> 09:59.932
at any time they lose their kids?

10:00.016 --> 10:02.268
-Dong-myeong! Honey!
-They all say the same thing.

10:02.351 --> 10:04.562
"It happened in the blink of an eye."

10:04.645 --> 10:07.773
They lost their child
in the blink of an eye.

10:14.238 --> 10:15.698
They found my son? Did they?

10:17.033 --> 10:17.867
Ae-sun.

10:18.367 --> 10:19.577
Did we find my son?

10:21.996 --> 10:22.955
Ae-sun.

10:28.294 --> 10:29.211
Ae-sun.

10:30.630 --> 10:31.672
What?

10:32.840 --> 10:33.758
What?

11:06.207 --> 11:07.291
Hospital.

11:08.501 --> 11:10.670
Dong-myeong needs to see the doctor.

11:11.921 --> 11:12.922
Oh boy.

11:14.131 --> 11:16.258
My baby, he's cold.

11:19.053 --> 11:21.681
Why isn't anyone calling an ambulance?

11:26.811 --> 11:27.728
Dong-myeong.

11:28.354 --> 11:29.188
Honey.

11:29.939 --> 11:30.773
Honey.

11:31.273 --> 11:32.108
Dear.

11:34.068 --> 11:34.902
Dong-myeong.

11:35.653 --> 11:36.570
Baby.

11:37.571 --> 11:38.406
Baby.

11:39.031 --> 11:40.408
What's wrong with you?

11:42.159 --> 11:43.202
Honey.

11:45.538 --> 11:46.580
We need

11:48.499 --> 11:50.835
to call the doctor. The doctor.

12:03.305 --> 12:05.808
Call for an ambulance, okay, Gwan-sik?

12:06.517 --> 12:07.518
Why

12:08.394 --> 12:10.438
won't anyone call for the ambulance?

12:11.772 --> 12:13.941
Just call for the ambulance,
why don't you?

12:31.375 --> 12:32.752
For the first time…

12:36.297 --> 12:38.674
…their Steelheart broke apart.

13:39.109 --> 13:40.694
My father's tears

13:41.487 --> 13:42.780
filled the seas.

15:07.406 --> 15:09.450
I should've hugged him.

15:14.330 --> 15:16.165
I should've hugged him.

15:18.250 --> 15:20.669
Her son,
who was with her at lunch,

15:21.670 --> 15:23.631
was no more by dinner.

15:25.925 --> 15:28.469
Mommy. Mommy!

15:28.552 --> 15:30.679
Mommy, give me a hug.

15:30.763 --> 15:32.890
Give me a hug.

15:32.973 --> 15:34.725
Mommy, I want a hug.

15:34.808 --> 15:37.561
Mommy, Mommy, give me a hug.

15:47.905 --> 15:49.490
I should've hugged him.

16:14.848 --> 16:16.183
At the funeral,

16:16.684 --> 16:20.145
Grandma never accused Mom of anything.

16:20.229 --> 16:23.273
She just said that a mother
who lost her child

16:23.357 --> 16:25.275
has more tears than the sea.

16:37.830 --> 16:38.914
Move on.

16:40.165 --> 16:41.250
What choice do you have?

16:42.876 --> 16:46.088
You have two children
who still need you to be their mother.

16:49.842 --> 16:51.802
Life will move on if you let it.

16:52.302 --> 16:53.762
Life goes on.

16:56.015 --> 16:57.391
Life goes on.

16:58.142 --> 17:00.561
There will be days when life is hard.

17:01.854 --> 17:04.189
Once in a while, there may be days

17:04.273 --> 17:06.442
you feel like
giving up on life altogether.

17:06.525 --> 17:10.112
I said stop talking!
I won't agree to that!

17:10.696 --> 17:12.781
I won't eat the abalone!

17:16.910 --> 17:18.454
Oh, my little girl.

17:20.456 --> 17:22.166
When will you understand?

17:33.093 --> 17:33.927
Ae-sun,

17:34.803 --> 17:37.598
if you ever feel like giving up on life,

17:37.681 --> 17:40.142
think about my life as a haenyeo.

17:43.353 --> 17:45.272
People who make their living on land

17:45.355 --> 17:48.317
say they want to die so easily
when things get rough.

17:49.485 --> 17:51.361
No matter how upset or agonizing life is,

17:51.945 --> 17:54.573
they can't speak lightly of death
in front of a haenyeo.

17:55.908 --> 17:59.661
I've faced death hundreds of times
in those powerful waters,

17:59.745 --> 18:03.207
and each time, I found
hundreds of reasons to keep living.

18:03.290 --> 18:04.958
So keep on living.

18:05.584 --> 18:06.835
Keep on living.

18:07.711 --> 18:09.713
Why die with so many reasons to live?

18:12.925 --> 18:15.803
When your body's tired
and your heart wants to give up,

18:16.762 --> 18:18.639
there will be days

18:18.722 --> 18:20.599
when you want to give up on life.

18:21.183 --> 18:22.476
Refuse to back down.

18:23.435 --> 18:24.770
Fight to pick yourself back up.

18:25.354 --> 18:27.147
Take out a blanket and stomp on it.

18:27.231 --> 18:28.690
Till your soil.

18:28.774 --> 18:30.192
Go earn your money.

18:30.776 --> 18:34.780
If you tell yourself,
"I won't die. I'm gonna survive,"

18:34.863 --> 18:37.491
and use your arms and legs to push you up,

18:39.034 --> 18:41.370
you'll get past the dark waters

18:43.080 --> 18:44.957
and finally see the sky.

18:47.835 --> 18:49.628
By then, you'll breathe again.

19:14.862 --> 19:17.656
-Do you know how to do it?
-No, I don't.

19:17.739 --> 19:19.074
This will be sweet, right?

19:24.830 --> 19:25.873
Ooh.

19:26.623 --> 19:28.041
Ooh, it looks yummy.

19:40.637 --> 19:42.556
Is that what you wanted to eat?

19:45.684 --> 19:47.769
Is that the food you craved?

19:52.524 --> 19:54.568
Hey, speak to me. What's going on?

19:56.570 --> 19:57.905
Are you mad at Mommy?

20:43.617 --> 20:44.952
Yang Eun-myeong.

20:45.619 --> 20:47.955
I asked you why you won't talk to me, son.

20:51.667 --> 20:53.794
Never gonna talk to me again, is that it?

21:27.995 --> 21:31.790
SCHOOL SUPPORT FEES DUE BY THE 20TH

21:47.180 --> 21:49.433
Why didn't you say
you got a perfect score?

21:51.435 --> 21:53.687
Why'd you keep it a secret from me, honey?

22:00.110 --> 22:01.653
Geum-myeong.

22:04.698 --> 22:05.532
Hey.

22:06.408 --> 22:07.617
Are you mad at Mommy?

22:08.327 --> 22:10.329
So mad you won't say anything?

22:11.830 --> 22:12.873
Is it because…

22:14.875 --> 22:16.043
is it because…

22:19.755 --> 22:21.340
…I didn't save your little brother?

22:22.883 --> 22:25.385
Are you mad at me?
Is that why you're not talking?

22:27.346 --> 22:29.514
It's because you are mad at me, Mom.

22:32.392 --> 22:33.393
What?

22:34.311 --> 22:36.480
I left my brother alone.

22:37.522 --> 22:39.107
That's why he's dead.

22:48.533 --> 22:49.368
It's 'cause…

22:50.827 --> 22:51.995
it's 'cause

22:53.330 --> 22:55.207
I went out there on the bike.

22:55.957 --> 23:00.003
If I never left to ride the bike,
Dong-myeong would still be alive.

23:00.087 --> 23:01.338
It's 'cause

23:02.547 --> 23:05.342
I wouldn't listen when I was told not to

23:06.510 --> 23:08.637
because a typhoon was coming.

23:09.137 --> 23:13.016
Dong-myeong died
because I still went to go riding.

23:17.729 --> 23:18.897
That was when

23:20.148 --> 23:21.358
Mom and Dad

23:22.359 --> 23:24.069
came to their senses.

23:28.990 --> 23:30.033
I'm sorry.

23:31.618 --> 23:32.786
I'm so sorry.

23:33.995 --> 23:34.871
I'm sorry.

23:36.248 --> 23:37.541
It's all my fault.

23:38.458 --> 23:39.918
I'm sorry, Eun-myeong.

24:10.407 --> 24:11.241
I'll do it.

24:14.828 --> 24:18.415
The Steelheart
picked himself up after three days.

24:18.498 --> 24:20.500
He finished his breakfast

24:21.751 --> 24:23.253
and went out to sea.

24:24.337 --> 24:25.338
Hmm.

24:38.435 --> 24:40.937
Geum-myeong, tell your teacher

24:41.938 --> 24:44.566
I'll pay your school fees
in three days, okay?

24:50.363 --> 24:51.198
Hmm?

24:53.867 --> 24:57.037
They had three days
to mourn. That's all.

24:58.747 --> 25:00.332
Only three days.

25:04.544 --> 25:08.048
Dad,
what are you gonna catch today?

25:08.673 --> 25:09.508
Croaker.

25:10.467 --> 25:11.343
Summer croaker.

25:12.511 --> 25:14.262
-Croaker?
-Mm.

25:15.138 --> 25:17.390
I'll bring them home
instead of selling them.

25:18.183 --> 25:19.476
-Bring them back?
-Yeah.

25:21.102 --> 25:21.937
Let's

25:22.771 --> 25:24.022
all eat together tonight.

25:25.232 --> 25:27.150
Let's all eat together as a family.

26:20.620 --> 26:22.330
Wanna come eat with us?

26:22.414 --> 26:24.624
She sold everything.
She's packing up.

26:25.542 --> 26:29.212
Well, she has her back to the sea,
but business is good.

26:30.630 --> 26:34.009
She says that
she doesn't want to even look at the sea.

26:35.635 --> 26:37.596
The skies are so clear today.

26:38.430 --> 26:39.889
Seeing it this clear,

26:40.557 --> 26:44.060
as if nothing ever happened,
makes her want to vomit.

26:48.440 --> 26:52.569
Her mother, her father,
and now the sea takes her son.

26:52.652 --> 26:55.113
Imagine how she feels
earning a living at the sea.

26:55.196 --> 26:56.072
Goddamn.

26:57.782 --> 27:00.660
She has to live
with all of that heartache.

27:02.912 --> 27:05.915
The sea god is a sadistic one.

27:05.999 --> 27:08.251
He stole everything she held dear

27:08.918 --> 27:11.254
but tells her,
"I'll keep you alive, I think."

27:12.005 --> 27:14.341
So he still gives her all kinds of things.

27:14.841 --> 27:16.343
I'm thankful to her.

27:17.427 --> 27:19.596
I'm thankful she's moving on.

27:20.805 --> 27:22.599
Did you sell all the squid?

27:23.558 --> 27:25.602
We managed to catch
a convict grouper today.

27:26.353 --> 27:30.398
If we sell that one,
we can get 1,000 won, easy.

27:35.070 --> 27:37.197
We can even buy Eun-myeong a new backpack.

27:37.947 --> 27:39.783
It's so unfair.

27:45.205 --> 27:46.831
So unfair.

27:55.423 --> 27:57.300
Geum-myeong. Eun-myeong. Let's go.

28:14.359 --> 28:16.027
I don't wanna be

28:17.612 --> 28:19.948
around the sea for any reason at all.

28:21.866 --> 28:24.285
It's so unfair.

28:27.997 --> 28:28.832
Ae-sun,

28:30.667 --> 28:31.835
let's stop crying.

28:34.462 --> 28:36.089
If Mom and Dad keep crying,

28:37.215 --> 28:38.258
it'll affect the kids.

28:39.175 --> 28:40.635
They'll always be anxious.

28:41.386 --> 28:44.431
I want this summer to be over already.

28:46.057 --> 28:48.226
Pretty annoying how erratic it is.

28:49.686 --> 28:51.646
If it's hot, it's way too hot.

28:52.480 --> 28:54.441
When it rains, it pours.

28:56.151 --> 28:59.070
Summer lets nature grow lush,
but the next thing you know,

28:59.738 --> 29:03.283
it brings storms and crushes everything,
and we're helpless.

29:04.033 --> 29:05.702
The two-faced summer

29:06.286 --> 29:08.163
brought my young parents

29:08.246 --> 29:09.831
down to their knees.

29:10.874 --> 29:13.334
Why does it have to be so aggressive?

29:14.627 --> 29:17.005
If it were me, I'd cut me some slack.

29:17.088 --> 29:19.174
Hey, watch out for that hole there.

29:19.257 --> 29:20.425
No problem.

29:20.508 --> 29:22.135
We all give beginners a break.

29:24.429 --> 29:26.055
But it's a first for me too.

29:28.600 --> 29:30.935
Why am I not getting a break
from the sea god?

29:32.103 --> 29:35.190
Like grass
that was pressed down by the typhoon…

29:35.690 --> 29:37.358
How can we move on now?

29:38.485 --> 29:41.404
…she was knocked down,
but she got back up again.

29:41.488 --> 29:42.530
Still,

29:43.573 --> 29:45.825
life goes on despite the summer's whims.

29:48.453 --> 29:51.414
Grass and trees that are knocked down
by the summer typhoon,

29:52.582 --> 29:53.666
they'll get up again.

29:56.336 --> 29:58.880
Rain can fall
and just sweep away everything.

30:00.965 --> 30:03.218
Ah, but once the sun shines again,

30:04.302 --> 30:05.929
everything comes back to life.

30:06.429 --> 30:08.139
All things on land and sea.

30:12.393 --> 30:13.853
What if I can't move on?

30:16.689 --> 30:19.943
I think moving on
could be a thing I can't do.

30:23.071 --> 30:24.656
There are crabs here.

30:24.739 --> 30:25.907
Our kids need to live on.

30:25.990 --> 30:27.367
-Where?
-Here.

30:27.450 --> 30:29.160
You can't catch that one.

30:35.166 --> 30:36.167
Gwan-sik.

30:43.174 --> 30:44.676
I have caused it all.

30:46.344 --> 30:48.137
I was the one who put…

30:52.141 --> 30:53.852
Dong-myeong on the seawall.

31:03.903 --> 31:06.948
On his first birthday,
I carried him on my back or in my arms

31:07.031 --> 31:09.284
so we could all meet you on that seawall.

31:12.161 --> 31:14.706
I lined up the kids and told them,

31:16.332 --> 31:18.835
"If we stand up here, Dad will come soon."

31:23.214 --> 31:25.425
I said no matter how bad the storm is…

31:27.552 --> 31:29.679
you would return to us if we waited there.

31:39.397 --> 31:41.024
I told them that.

31:45.361 --> 31:47.030
Our baby, Dong-myeong…

31:51.910 --> 31:53.244
…died because of me.

32:00.960 --> 32:02.170
It's all my fault.

32:08.676 --> 32:11.554
If you have to assign blame,
then look to the heavens and sea instead.

32:17.644 --> 32:19.187
It's not your fault at all.

32:19.270 --> 32:20.855
Hmm?

32:22.774 --> 32:25.193
Look, nobody in our family
is to blame. No one.

32:27.195 --> 32:30.114
Dad kept telling himself
no one was to blame,

32:30.198 --> 32:33.034
but on the inside, he did resent someone.

32:34.577 --> 32:37.664
Mom said she found out
who it was Dad resented

32:38.164 --> 32:40.041
about 30 years later.

32:48.299 --> 32:49.133
Hey.

32:49.634 --> 32:51.344
ENDOSCOPY CENTER

32:51.427 --> 32:54.389
Do you know what it is your dad uttered?

32:57.392 --> 32:58.977
Um, he muttered nonsense or what?

32:59.727 --> 33:01.521
People do that in endoscopy.

33:07.151 --> 33:10.238
What, did he talk about
another woman?

33:15.284 --> 33:16.327
Barrier.

33:17.578 --> 33:18.871
Huh? Barrier?

33:19.998 --> 33:20.832
Gwan-sik!

33:21.582 --> 33:23.167
Gwan-sik!

33:23.251 --> 33:25.837
He was muttering the words,

33:27.505 --> 33:30.008
"I shouldn't have gone
to build the barrier."

33:30.967 --> 33:32.385
"I shouldn't have gone."

33:36.097 --> 33:39.434
He's very much like steel
in every way.

33:40.018 --> 33:42.353
Once something truly gets into the man,

33:42.437 --> 33:44.439
he just locks it inside.

33:46.065 --> 33:47.650
I don't know how he coped with it.

33:48.693 --> 33:50.486
How did he cope with all that?

33:54.532 --> 33:55.950
Should he have packed it in?

33:57.076 --> 34:01.748
Uh-uh, there were still
two pairs of twinkling eyes watching us.

34:04.542 --> 34:06.627
So we saved both you and Dad?

34:07.545 --> 34:09.005
Absolutely, you did.

34:10.339 --> 34:11.674
You did save us.

34:17.555 --> 34:19.474
If it weren't for you…

34:20.391 --> 34:21.934
If it weren't you…

34:23.269 --> 34:26.647
NAME OF THE DECEASED: YANG DONG-MYEONG

34:32.445 --> 34:36.240
HOUSEHOLDER: YANG GWAN-SIK

34:37.992 --> 34:41.579
RELATIONSHIP TO HOUSEHOLDER: SON

34:46.459 --> 34:49.879
DATE OF BIRTH: SEPTEMBER 6, 1974

34:54.342 --> 34:59.055
3 YEARS OLD

35:21.828 --> 35:25.248
You can't imagine
what it feels like to lose a child.

35:29.919 --> 35:32.588
He couldn't cry openly anywhere.

35:33.422 --> 35:36.092
He was completely broken on the inside.

35:50.314 --> 35:52.692
Dalgona doesn't have much nutrition.

35:55.820 --> 35:57.572
I ate my food. I promise I did.

35:57.655 --> 35:59.949
Jeez, here.

36:07.707 --> 36:11.085
Oh,
I wondered how we could move on.

36:12.295 --> 36:14.755
What in the world did he eat?

36:18.551 --> 36:20.386
Mom, I've been eating every day.

36:20.469 --> 36:22.763
They even bring us meat most of the time.

36:32.231 --> 36:34.150
We were able to move on

36:34.233 --> 36:38.029
because there were people
who fed the children for us.

36:40.531 --> 36:42.700
A canola flower never blooms by itself.

36:42.783 --> 36:45.203
You always see a field of canola flowers.

36:45.703 --> 36:47.163
Had I been on my own,

36:47.246 --> 36:49.415
I would've been broken
a hundred times over.

36:54.629 --> 36:57.340
You know,
as the saying goes,

36:58.216 --> 37:01.636
it takes a village
to keep one person alive.

37:15.107 --> 37:18.694
They're fine. They'll be fine.
With the stove on, they're okay, I think.

37:23.324 --> 37:24.951
Don't make it too obvious.

37:25.034 --> 37:26.994
They might not like
all that kindness and help.

37:27.078 --> 37:28.871
Should we not give them those?

37:28.955 --> 37:30.539
They're today's first eggs.

37:32.500 --> 37:34.710
Give them the first eggs,
then they'll give them strength.

37:35.211 --> 37:37.880
Don't keep me
from giving them eggs.

37:37.964 --> 37:40.341
You're the one
who gave away all of our rice.

37:40.424 --> 37:42.969
You gave them all our octopuses. You did!

37:49.475 --> 37:52.770
So I was wondering
if I could get a little…

37:54.480 --> 37:55.731
…rice, you know.

37:55.815 --> 37:57.858
I don't understand.
What are you saying, dear?

37:57.942 --> 38:00.236
What are you complaining about?

38:00.319 --> 38:02.280
There's plenty of folks worse off.

38:10.496 --> 38:11.622
But is it you?

38:12.999 --> 38:14.041
The rice jar?

38:15.334 --> 38:18.671
Well, I have no idea what you mean,
crybaby woman.

38:21.632 --> 38:25.177
Why are you saying
you don't have any idea? I know you do.

38:25.261 --> 38:29.765
'Cause, for some reason,
that empty jar is never completely empty.

38:37.857 --> 38:40.651
I saw that the rice jar
was empty before I slept.

38:40.735 --> 38:42.403
I know what I saw.

38:56.083 --> 38:59.128
Every morning,
there's a little more, then a little more.

38:59.211 --> 39:00.046
Hmm?

39:00.921 --> 39:04.050
I thought maybe I didn't see very well
because it was night,

39:04.133 --> 39:06.469
but it went beyond a day or two.

39:06.552 --> 39:09.055
There's just enough for a family of three.

39:09.555 --> 39:11.349
It's just so strange.

39:12.058 --> 39:14.560
Just enough to keep us guessing.

39:14.643 --> 39:16.187
It's the exact amount we need.

39:19.648 --> 39:20.941
Oh, why do I bother?

39:21.567 --> 39:22.902
Why do I bother?

39:27.198 --> 39:29.492
It's not some magical jar,

39:29.575 --> 39:30.576
and I'm not a dummy.

39:30.659 --> 39:32.578
She got a migraine figuring it out.

39:32.661 --> 39:35.873
If she just gave it to you,
you wouldn't take it, Ae-sun.

39:35.956 --> 39:40.211
So then she really tried to give it
without you knowing about it.

39:40.294 --> 39:42.338
Um, but… Well, if it gave her a migraine--

39:42.421 --> 39:45.800
Who would want to watch
a pregnant woman go hungry?

39:49.720 --> 39:51.347
Go steam the octopuses.

39:51.430 --> 39:53.099
Somebody gave them to me.

39:54.266 --> 39:57.311
You absolutely don't have to do this
for my mom's ancestral rites.

39:57.395 --> 40:01.107
If you don't add octopus to her table,
your mom will come beat you down.

40:02.400 --> 40:05.152
No haenyeo goes diving by herself.

40:05.778 --> 40:07.071
When you're about to

40:07.571 --> 40:10.116
lose your breath in the deep, dark waters,

40:10.199 --> 40:13.661
well, you have got to be
very near other divers.

40:13.744 --> 40:16.205
Otherwise, you won't be able
to breathe again.

40:17.081 --> 40:19.125
No one's an island.
Let's go together.

40:19.208 --> 40:20.918
If you go with others,

40:21.001 --> 40:23.587
a hundred miles
will feel like ten miles, my dear.

40:23.671 --> 40:29.760
GO TOGETHER, WITH OTHERS.
IF YOU DO, 100 MILES WILL FEEL LIKE TEN.

40:35.433 --> 40:37.810
Gyeong-ja, that is Ae-sun's.

40:39.687 --> 40:41.564
Ae-sun is having the baby soon.

40:41.647 --> 40:43.190
I'm gonna give it to her.

40:43.274 --> 40:45.526
I wanted to touch it a bit
because it has been a while,

40:45.609 --> 40:48.237
so I just wanted
to feel it a little. There.

40:48.320 --> 40:50.698
Right? They're pretty.

40:52.116 --> 40:54.785
-Oh, she is something, isn't she?
-Hey, did you rinse this?

40:54.869 --> 40:56.036
It's so cold.

40:58.664 --> 41:01.792
Can you write
"For Moral Support"?

41:02.877 --> 41:05.754
If you write that for me,
she'll definitely get it.

41:12.803 --> 41:16.765
"For Moral Support," okay?
Hmm? Mm-hmm.

41:21.187 --> 41:22.438
Works for you?

41:22.521 --> 41:25.941
DO HUI-JEONG SCHOLARSHIP
10,000 WON

41:28.444 --> 41:29.737
Is it wrong?

41:29.820 --> 41:32.907
Three months of rent
to go to the baby's family, right?

41:43.125 --> 41:44.502
Can you read, lady?

41:49.715 --> 41:51.342
One, two, three, four.

41:51.425 --> 41:53.135
One, ten, hundred, thousand.

41:55.387 --> 41:56.764
Fine, yes.

41:56.847 --> 41:57.723
Makes sense.

42:05.022 --> 42:05.856
If only

42:07.066 --> 42:08.984
I'd never hidden in that small closet.

42:09.068 --> 42:09.902
Ah shit.

42:09.985 --> 42:12.029
Why did you pay their rent, huh?

42:12.947 --> 42:16.867
It's my destiny to live with
overly giving boss ladies, I guess.

42:18.202 --> 42:20.079
Should you be saying that? Huh?

42:20.162 --> 42:21.163
Sure, why not?

42:21.247 --> 42:23.791
I deserve to be slapped
for what I've done back then,

42:24.291 --> 42:26.168
but you're not guilty of anything.

42:26.252 --> 42:27.753
Since when is love a sin?

42:28.837 --> 42:31.131
Just cut the nonsense

42:31.215 --> 42:34.093
and straighten your priorities out,
all right?

42:34.176 --> 42:36.387
There's nothing complicated about karma.

42:36.470 --> 42:38.013
Animals bring up animals.

42:38.097 --> 42:39.932
Nobles breed nobles, huh?

42:40.015 --> 42:43.769
Kids inherit
their parents' imperfections exactly.

42:43.852 --> 42:46.188
Min-ok, stop.

42:46.772 --> 42:48.232
She must've really hated me.

42:49.191 --> 42:52.319
Her adolescence was ruined
once I joined the family.

42:52.403 --> 42:55.823
It's pretty sneaky of me to think
I can make it up to her with 10,000 won.

42:55.906 --> 42:58.909
-I gave her a whole cabbage field, okay?
-Oh, that rock field, right?

42:58.993 --> 42:59.952
That field of dog shit?

43:00.035 --> 43:03.038
It was Ae-sun's small hands
that plowed that field.

43:03.122 --> 43:04.248
And on top of that,

43:04.331 --> 43:07.293
that field's original owner
was her mother, Byeong-cheol.

43:08.294 --> 43:09.211
Min-ok.

43:09.295 --> 43:11.547
Talk the shit you want,
but keep your conscience straight.

43:11.630 --> 43:13.090
Yapping doesn't justify a thing.

43:13.173 --> 43:15.968
Min-ok, I told you to quit it.
I'm getting angry.

43:17.052 --> 43:18.804
Now that I've raised our kids,

43:18.887 --> 43:20.764
you should've paid for all of

43:21.265 --> 43:23.892
Ae-sun's college tuition
because she truly deserved it.

43:23.976 --> 43:26.395
Ooh! Come on, yeah, college!

43:26.478 --> 43:27.730
Go! Go! Go!

43:28.314 --> 43:29.898
She can go now if she wants.

43:29.982 --> 43:32.192
I'll pay for her,
even if I have to take out a loan!

43:32.276 --> 43:35.321
Why would she go to college now?
How? By what means?

43:35.404 --> 43:38.699
Hey, if she gets in,
I'll pay her tuition. Tell her!

43:39.658 --> 43:41.827
Don't say anything if she doesn't get in.

43:41.910 --> 43:45.205
She doesn't need college to be a captain,
a deputy chief, or anything like that.

43:46.540 --> 43:49.209
If she goes to Seoul,
she'll only be cut down to size.

43:49.752 --> 43:52.421
The best she'll get
is a doctorate.

43:52.504 --> 43:54.173
She'll just drain the family's wallet.

43:54.256 --> 43:57.801
All we'll do is hang banners around town
to show off which college accepted her.

43:57.885 --> 43:59.678
I never saw the big deal anyway.

44:02.306 --> 44:04.099
Hi, Geum-myeong.

44:07.603 --> 44:09.229
Oh, oh, it's her.

44:13.317 --> 44:15.235
Did you make it?

44:15.861 --> 44:16.987
Did you not?

44:17.738 --> 44:19.448
Oh, Mom.

44:19.531 --> 44:21.784
If I didn't get in, who would?

44:23.369 --> 44:24.828
Look, look, look!

44:24.912 --> 44:27.247
"Yang Geum-myeong." It's written here.

44:28.957 --> 44:30.417
Oh my God. Wow.

44:32.753 --> 44:35.130
Hey! Sell the boat! Sell it!

44:37.800 --> 44:40.302
You did it. You did it for real, honey.

44:42.971 --> 44:46.767
I… don't know
if it's okay for me to say this.

44:46.850 --> 44:48.143
I never

44:49.478 --> 44:52.523
thought that I would say this ever again.

44:53.315 --> 44:55.192
-I…
-You're glad?

44:58.112 --> 44:58.946
Yes.

45:00.030 --> 45:01.573
I'm feeling so happy.

45:04.284 --> 45:05.786
So glad.

45:08.706 --> 45:09.915
CERTIFICATE OF ADMISSION

45:09.998 --> 45:13.502
Okay, one, two, three.

45:14.461 --> 45:15.295
Ah!

45:18.006 --> 45:19.174
BOARDING HOUSE AVAILABLE

45:19.258 --> 45:20.384
AFFORDABLE ROOM FOR RENT

45:20.467 --> 45:21.802
RENT NEAR SNU
AFFORDABLE ROOM

45:24.763 --> 45:26.807
Geum-myeong! Geum-myeong!

45:38.610 --> 45:40.487
Your daughter's name is Geum-myeong?

45:40.571 --> 45:42.823
We have one in our family.

45:44.867 --> 45:46.618
Your son's name is Geum-myeong?

45:46.702 --> 45:47.911
Oh, no.

45:47.995 --> 45:48.954
It's me.

45:49.997 --> 45:51.039
I am Geum-myeong.

45:52.040 --> 45:53.417
I'm Park Geum-myeong.

45:53.500 --> 45:55.502
Oh!

45:58.046 --> 46:00.340
Wow, what an interesting coincidence.

46:00.424 --> 46:01.925
YALASHANG FILM CLUB

46:02.009 --> 46:03.218
Should we get some noodles?

46:03.302 --> 46:06.889
So what's your major, huh? What is it?

46:06.972 --> 46:08.474
Oh, um, law.

46:08.557 --> 46:11.769
Let's go have noodles. Hurry up.
Let's take the picture and just go.

46:11.852 --> 46:13.479
Here. I can take it for you.

46:13.562 --> 46:16.064
-If you all want to stand there.
-Ooh, that's nice of you.

46:16.774 --> 46:18.901
Okay, you take ours, and I'll take yours.

46:18.984 --> 46:20.903
Whose picture? Why are you taking theirs?

46:20.986 --> 46:23.071
Let's take it. Come on.

46:24.406 --> 46:26.658
Thank you.

46:28.118 --> 46:28.952
Mm.

46:29.036 --> 46:29.870
Here we go.

46:30.370 --> 46:31.663
One, two, three.

46:33.791 --> 46:35.584
Okay, I'll take one more.

46:39.171 --> 46:40.172
Smile.

46:42.007 --> 46:44.051
One, two, three!

46:45.260 --> 46:46.970
I said I didn't like him.

46:47.930 --> 46:50.140
I told you
I didn't like that guy at all, didn't I?

46:50.808 --> 46:51.850
Why not?

46:59.733 --> 47:01.485
Those weren't intended to be solo shots.

47:02.069 --> 47:05.280
Park Geum-myeong's son
was hitting on Geum-myeong.

47:05.364 --> 47:06.323
Hitting on her!

47:06.949 --> 47:08.325
Okay, I'll take one more.

47:10.661 --> 47:11.703
Okay, smile.

47:13.622 --> 47:16.375
One, two, three.

47:16.458 --> 47:18.335
Oh, so you feel annoyed now?

47:18.418 --> 47:20.087
Hey, let's call Geum-myeong.

47:20.170 --> 47:22.840
Why? You believe they ran off to Busan?

47:23.423 --> 47:24.883
Why would they go to Busan?

47:24.967 --> 47:26.051
Jeez.

47:26.134 --> 47:29.972
You pulled someone else's daughter there,
and you won't let your daughter go?

47:30.055 --> 47:31.598
Oh, I pulled you there?

47:31.682 --> 47:34.142
Jeez, I think you might
have a heart attack

47:34.226 --> 47:36.395
if she ever wanted to get married.

47:36.478 --> 47:38.355
Why would she get married?

47:46.989 --> 47:48.657
I'm telling you ahead of time.

47:50.534 --> 47:51.910
I can't go tomorrow.

47:54.204 --> 47:55.038
Oh.

47:56.331 --> 47:57.165
That's fine.

47:58.208 --> 47:59.626
You have class tomorrow.

48:01.461 --> 48:03.255
No way I can get to Nonsan.

48:04.131 --> 48:05.048
I can't.

48:07.175 --> 48:08.302
Take your mom.

48:10.804 --> 48:11.763
Mm.

48:12.931 --> 48:13.974
It's fine.

48:15.851 --> 48:17.394
Go with Oh Ye-rim.

48:18.270 --> 48:19.479
Why would I go with her?

48:21.231 --> 48:23.817
Anyway, I can't go. You know?

48:25.319 --> 48:26.153
I get it.

48:27.863 --> 48:30.407
-I'm saying I can't go.
-I said I get it.

48:30.490 --> 48:32.200
Damn it, you don't get it.

48:32.284 --> 48:33.702
Well, what do you mean?

48:34.870 --> 48:36.705
What am I saying if I can't go?

48:39.458 --> 48:40.542
Tonight is

48:41.585 --> 48:43.128
our last night together.

48:44.713 --> 48:47.132
Man, it means it's our last night!

48:48.884 --> 48:52.512
Keep her in check.
Your daughter is just like you.

48:52.596 --> 48:54.431
I swear I'm going to, damn it.

48:54.514 --> 48:55.724
What's wrong with you?

48:56.350 --> 48:58.936
A chip off the old block, Oh Ae-sun.

49:00.437 --> 49:03.398
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

49:07.069 --> 49:08.487
Sweetie.

49:15.744 --> 49:17.496
That's nice, isn't it?

49:18.580 --> 49:19.498
Mm.

49:20.999 --> 49:23.752
Is it a lot more expensive
to live on higher floors?

49:25.796 --> 49:27.172
They're full right now, she said.

49:27.255 --> 49:28.590
You believe her?

49:29.675 --> 49:31.551
Well, she's not a sweet talker,

49:31.635 --> 49:32.719
but she's the eldest.

49:32.803 --> 49:35.764
She's always too careful,
even if I tell her not to be.

49:35.847 --> 49:37.015
Jeez.

49:37.099 --> 49:40.102
Why do people in Seoul
have rooms in basements, you think?

49:40.602 --> 49:45.232
Hmm. My heart would break
if my baby was forced to live there.

49:49.736 --> 49:50.862
Will we be able

49:51.446 --> 49:53.031
to sell the cabbage field?

49:54.533 --> 49:56.159
Just leave the field.

49:57.035 --> 49:58.704
But you believe it'll sell?

49:58.787 --> 50:00.247
And stop selling things.

50:01.665 --> 50:03.583
Why? You wanna keep it?

50:04.334 --> 50:06.586
If we sell it all,
you'll have nothing left.

50:07.087 --> 50:10.382
Jeez, your wife over your daughter, huh?

50:13.635 --> 50:15.429
You know, looking back at it all,

50:16.263 --> 50:17.723
those days were nice.

50:19.016 --> 50:20.851
That was the best summer we had.

50:22.352 --> 50:24.646
Everything was so new back then.

50:25.480 --> 50:28.108
Even though it all felt
awkward and difficult,

50:28.191 --> 50:30.235
it was all new and exciting.

50:31.236 --> 50:33.238
I loved everything, you know.

50:42.914 --> 50:44.124
First love,

50:45.417 --> 50:46.626
our honeymoon…

50:48.628 --> 50:50.297
our first house,

50:50.380 --> 50:51.590
first boat,

50:52.382 --> 50:53.216
first full net.

50:54.301 --> 50:56.011
First child.

50:56.762 --> 50:58.513
Having our first child.

50:59.848 --> 51:01.224
Words escape me.

51:04.853 --> 51:06.897
Still leave the cabbage field, Ae-sun.

51:18.450 --> 51:20.452
Just leave the cabbage field.

51:21.369 --> 51:25.082
That field is your reward
for surviving that summer.

51:28.293 --> 51:30.712
I wondered how we could move forward.

51:32.255 --> 51:34.382
But life really just went on.

51:34.466 --> 51:36.718
Hey, Mom, look at this!

51:36.802 --> 51:39.221
Life went on and on.

51:39.888 --> 51:42.808
LIFE GOES ON AND ON

54:33.228 --> 54:37.857
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."
